## Why This Is Asked

Evaluates practical fintech security decisions: key management, rotating keys, PKCE, mTLS, replay protection, and observability trade-offs.

## Key Concepts

- OAuth2-like flows with PKCE
- JWT rotation and key management (HSM backing)
- mTLS and token binding
- Replay protection (nonce, jti)
- Observability, rate limits, and revocation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Token verification sketch
function verifyToken(token, keystore) {
  const { header } = parseJwt(token);
  const key = keystore.getKey(header.kid);
  const payload = verifyJwt(token, key);
  if (!payload) return false;
  if (payload.exp * 1000 < Date.now()) return false;
  return payload.aud.includes("api");
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test key rotation without downtime?
- How would you detect token abuse and adapt rate limits?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical ability to diagnose production rollouts with service meshes and canaries, focusing on end-to-end validation, live traffic checks, and safe rollback.

## Key Concepts
- Canary/rollout health in Istio
- Rollout status and events
- Readiness/Liveness probes relevance
- Safe rollback without downtime
- Synthetic traffic validation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal helper to parse rollout JSON and extract canary status (pseudo, for illustration)
function getCanaryStatus(rolloutJson) {
  try {
    const r = JSON.parse(rolloutJson);
    return r?.status?.canary?.traffic || 0;
  } catch {
    return 0;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you automate the rollback decision with a health-check gate?
- What metrics would you collect to prove P95 stability during rollback?
